config BR2_PACKAGE_REFORGE_ZRAM
	bool "reforge-zram"
	depends on BR2_LINUX_KERNEL
	depends on BR2_arm
	help
	  Builds zsmalloc.ko and zram.ko kernel modules from
	  the Allwinner T113 vendor BSP, vermagic 5.4.61 SMP preempt mod_unload
	  ARMv7 p2v8.  Also builds swapon_prio, a static armv7 helper that
	  calls swapon(2) with SWAP_FLAG_PREFER|priority (busybox swapon lacks
	  -p).

	  The private vendor BSP build uses the captured stock configuration,
	  independently of the main kernel's device/QEMU configuration.
	  These modules require the stock 5.4.61 kernel ABI.

	  The S35zram init script loads the modules at boot, configures the
	  compression algorithm (default: zstd) and swap device size (default:
	  256M), and activates the swap at priority 100 so zram is preferred
	  over any eMMC overflow swapfile.
